{'symbol': 'AEP', 'date': '2022-03-21 10:00:00', 'title': 'TRAVERSE WIND ENERGY CENTER BEGINS DELIVERING SAVINGS TO CUSTOMERS', 'text': "THE 998-MW TRAVERSE PROJECT IS THE LARGEST SINGLE WIND FARM EVER BUILT AT ONE TIME IN NORTH AMERICA COLUMBUS, OHIO , MARCH 21, 2022 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- AMERICAN ELECTRIC POWER'S (NASDAQ: AEP) 998-MEGAWATT (MW) TRAVERSE WIND ENERGY CENTER, THE LARGEST SINGLE WIND FARM BUILT AT ONE TIME IN NORTH AMERICA AND ONE OF THE LARGEST WIND FACILITIES WORLDWIDE, IS NOW PROVIDING CLEAN ENERGY TO CUSTOMERS IN ARKANSAS, LOUISIANA AND OKLAHOMA. TRAVERSE IS EXPECTED TO GENERATE 3.8 MILLION MEGAWATT-HOURS ANNUALLY FOR AEP'S PUBLIC SERVICE COMPANY OF OKLAHOMA (PSO) AND SOUTHWESTERN ELECTRIC POWER COMPANY (SWEPCO) CUSTOMERS IN OKLAHOMA, ARKANSAS AND LOUISIANA."}